.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt TPM 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tpm
.Nd Trusted Platform Module
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd device tpm
.Cd options RANDOM_ENABLE_TPM
.Pp
In
.Xr device.hints 5 :
.Cd hint.tpm.0.at="isa"
.Cd hint.tpm.0.maddr="0xfed40000"
.Cd hint.tpm.0.msize="0x5000"
.Cd hint.tpm.1.at="isa"
.Cd hint.tpm.1.maddr="0xfed40000"
.Cd hint.tpm.1.msize="0x1000"
.Pp
In
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Cd tpm_load="YES"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides support for various trusted platform modules (TPM) that can
store cryptographic keys.
.Pp
The driver can be configured to use an IRQ by providing a free ISA
interrupt vector in
.Pa /boot/device.hints .
.Pp
When the kernel is configured with
.Cd "options RANDOM_ENABLE_TPM" ,
the driver periodically obtains random bytes from the TPM and supplies them
to
.Xr random 4 .
.Pp
On EFI systems with a TPM 1.2 or TPM 2.0 firmware event log,
.Xr loader.efi 8
preserves the log for the driver.
The root-readable
.Pa /dev/tpm0_eventlog
device provides the raw TCG binary event log.
TCG2-format logs include final events recorded while exiting EFI boot
services.
Legacy SHA-1 logs, including those obtained through the TCG2 protocol,
are captured through the last entry reported before exiting boot services.
Events appended afterward are omitted.
In particular, EDK2 firmware measures the invocation and success of
ExitBootServices into PCR 5 after this snapshot, so replaying the saved
legacy log will not reproduce the final PCR 5 value on that firmware.
The legacy EFI TCG protocol provides neither a final-events table nor a
log truncation indicator.
.Pp
Each open has an independent read position and reaches end of file
after the saved log.
Reading the log does not issue TPM commands or change PCRs.
No event-log device is created if the firmware log is absent or invalid.
A firmware-reported truncated log is exported with a boot-time warning;
it may not reproduce the TPM's PCR values when replayed.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports the following trusted platform modules:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact -offset indent
.It
Atmel 97SC3203
.It
Broadcom BCM0102
.It
Infineon IFX SLD 9630 TT 1.1 and IFX SLB 9635 TT 1.2
.It
Intel INTC0102
.It
Sinosun SNS SSX35
.It
STM ST19WP18
.It
Winbond WEC WPCT200
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/tpm0_eventlog
.It Pa /dev/tpm0_eventlog
Read-only snapshot of the firmware event log.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Save the raw log for decoding or PCR replay by an event-log tool:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cat /dev/tpm0_eventlog > eventlog.bin
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr intro 4 ,
.Xr random 4 ,
.Xr device.hints 5 ,
.Xr config 8
.Pp
